  "statement": "(i) Evaluate $\\int x e^{x}\\,dx$ using integration by parts. (ii) Hence find $\\int_{0}^{1}x e^{x}\\,dx$. (iii) Evaluate $\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2}\\sin^{2}x\\,dx$.",
  "solution": "(i) Let $u=x,dv=e^{x}dx$: $\\int x e^{x}dx=x e^{x}-e^{x}+C=e^{x}(x-1)+C$. (ii) $[e^{x}(x-1)]_{0}^{1}=(0)-(-1)=1$. (iii) $\\sin^{2}x=\\frac{1-\\cos 2x}{2}$; $\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2}=\\bigl[\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\sin 2x}{4}\\bigr]_{0}^{\\pi/2}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.",
